816 0 obj
<<
/A 2524 0 R
/Alt (Diagram showing two processes for neural network attention mechanisms. Panel \(a\) illustrates modified channel attention, where input F undergoes global max pooling and average pooling, both sent to a shared multilayer perceptron, producing Mc and outputting as O to F. Panel \(b\) illustrates modified spatial attention, where input F prime passes through concatenated average and max operations, then separately through three convolution layers of sizes three by three, five by five, and seven by seven, combined with mean and standard deviation to generate Ms, then output as O times F prime to F double prime with residual addition.)
/K [90 2525 0 R]
/P 156 0 R
/Pg 52 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 4)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
